WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.640
The SCP Foundation has faced a number of wide,&nbsp;
potentially apocalyptic threats in its mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:13.760
to uphold normalcy and save humanity. We know the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation could be ruthless in this mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.000
the events of SCP-5000 before Agent Pietro&nbsp;
restarted the universe show what happens when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.640
the Foundation is pushed to its final decisions&nbsp;
regarding normalcy being upheld. In SCP-5000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.240
it seems that the SCP Foundation decided to cease&nbsp;
research further into the anomaly they needed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.800
neutralize, but what would have happened if they&nbsp;
didn’t? In any case, we know the SCP Foundation is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.560
dedicated to normalcy and the containment of&nbsp;
the anomalous, but what happens when the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:51.120
Foundation is faced with a dire decision:&nbsp;
uphold normalcy or destroy their universe.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.320
The multiverse is a concept in science fiction&nbsp;
that has gained mass amounts of popularity over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.800
recent years, especially recently, thanks to a&nbsp;
certain wall-crawler’s movie. Multiverses are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.480
parallel universes that are similar or extremely&nbsp;
different from the main ones. Scientists have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.680
pondered over the existence of a multiverse for&nbsp;
hundreds of years, with the most popular being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.520
Many Worlds Interpretation, a theory of quantum&nbsp;
mechanics that states there are many worlds that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.520
exist in parallel at the same space and time as&nbsp;
our own. Some interpretations even state that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:31.840
every decision a person makes causes a branch in&nbsp;
reality, where the person made the other decision.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:38.800
We’re familiar with the SCP Foundation’s run-ins&nbsp;
with the multiverse, from SCP-2935: O, Death, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.680
cave that allows the wanderer to enter a parallel&nbsp;
dimension that’s fully and completely dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.760
only for the same thing to happen to their&nbsp;
world once they return through the cave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:53.680
or SCP-1437, a hole that allows&nbsp;
the Foundation to send, receive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:02:00.320
and read parallel dimensional documentation&nbsp;
from other, multiversal SCP Foundations.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:07.840
Combine those two concepts with an SCP-001&nbsp;
proposal. The importance of an SCP-001 proposal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.720
is not lost on the Foundation. Researchers of&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation save the SCP-001 slot for only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:21.040
the most dangerous, apocalyptic, or widespread&nbsp;
anomalies that could affect the Foundation itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:28.080
humanity, and normalcy. Arbelict’s SCP-001&nbsp;
Proposal and the research within its file found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.400
the answer to the question we posed above, when&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation is faced with a dire decision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.680
do they uphold normalcy or destroy their&nbsp;
universe and all the people who live in it?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.760
The file begins somewhat different from&nbsp;
what we’re used to with SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.600
files. Instead of an item number or containment&nbsp;
procedures, we begin with a yellow notice from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.880
The Records And Information Security&nbsp;
Administration, or RAISA for short.&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:02.000
The notice states that the following file was&nbsp;
received in 2026 from dimension R-42. Is dimension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:09.680
R-42 potentially the cause of SCP-001? Could they&nbsp;
be attacking this version of the SCP Foundation?

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.440
The notice continues with a description&nbsp;
of the file that follows it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.880
it states the file below describes an anomaly&nbsp;
threatening all members of humankind in all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:25.760
the multiverse. This file had been emitted to this&nbsp;
version of the SCP Foundation for 8 minutes as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.760
extremely dangerous congitohazard, classified&nbsp;
as a class 5 cognitohazard capable of easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:37.200
destabilizing and penetrating this universe,&nbsp;
however, it was found to not be dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.240
only reading as a danger level 0. While this&nbsp;
Foundation was unable to quickly counteract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:48.320
this cognitohazard, it appeared to not pose a&nbsp;
threat to the affected universe’s humankind.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.960
Part of this notice is crossed out,&nbsp;
indicating that it is no longer true:

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.680
“There is a high threat of&nbsp;
repeated cognitohazardous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.200
or other forms of attack from dimension R-42”

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.840
Instead, this part has been&nbsp;
replaced with the following fact:

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.000
“dimension R-42 no longer exists.”

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.520
Did that version’s SCP Foundation fall&nbsp;
to SCP-001? Their entire universe no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.440
longer exists, so perhaps, this file that&nbsp;
this dimension’s SCP Foundation received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.800
could be a potential warning.
Under this RAISA notice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.840
the reader is not greeted with the standard&nbsp;
Foundation documentation yet again. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:34.480
it seems that the original senders of this file&nbsp;
left a note for the readers of this file. It says

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.960
“Greetings. You are reading this&nbsp;
dossier in a paradimension of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.880
the relict dimension R-42. Due to the&nbsp;
colossal size of your world's address,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.920
for your convenience, your dimension&nbsp;
will be hereafter referred to as "PD".”

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:56.640
Paradimensions? It seems as though we’re reading&nbsp;
this SCP-001 file through the eyes of the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:03.600
Foundation in this so-called Paradimension, so if&nbsp;
the original SCP Foundation and their universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.920
R-42, is now destroyed,&nbsp;
what does this mean for us?

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.280
The note continues:

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:15.840
“The following message has been constructed by&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation of the relict dimension R-42&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.000
and is addressed to the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation of paradimension PD.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:26.720
Enclosed you will find information about&nbsp;
SCP-001, which is a threat to the multiverse.”

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.720
Here we go, SCP-001 is definitely&nbsp;
the cause of R-42’s destruction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:39.760
But how can we be sure of this? Maybe SCP-001&nbsp;
caused the Foundation to destroy their universe?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.480
The note also includes the following statement:

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.440
“As you may have noticed, this message was&nbsp;
preceded by a burst signal containing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:53.200
non-dangerous cognitohazard. The burst signal was&nbsp;
constructed in such a way that minimal change to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:58.960
the signal would have caused indiscriminate and&nbsp;
overwhelming casualties among the denizens of PD.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:05.760
As you can see, R-42 is capable of eliminating&nbsp;
the absolute majority of PD denizens but has not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:12.320
exercised this capability. In the context above,&nbsp;
we ask you to consider this action not as an act&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:18.320
of aggression, but as a demonstration of the&nbsp;
fact that R-42 has no pretension for conquest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:24.320
or other forms of aggression towards PD.&nbsp;
Take the following information in earnest.”

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:28.560
Well, at least this version of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation is being someone friendly with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:34.800
the paradimension. If R-42’s SCP Foundation&nbsp;
needs to quell this multiversal threat though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:39.280
why are they leaving it up to an SCP&nbsp;
Foundation that may not be so inclined?

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:45.040
The SCP-001 file begins with the object&nbsp;
class. This anomaly is of the joint class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:53.600
of Paradox-Apollyon. We know from SCP-001 When Day&nbsp;
Breaks or SCP-3999 that Apollyon class anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:59.600
are extremely dangerous, posing an immediate&nbsp;
and almost unstoppable threat to normalcy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:07.680
the SCP Foundation, all of humanity, or even the&nbsp;
universe itself. The paradox part is interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:14.320
What exactly is paradoxical about an Apollyon&nbsp;
class anomaly? A footnote explains this for us:

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.960
“This anomaly's distinguishing feature is that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.440
in order to eliminate the anomaly that&nbsp;
will inevitably eliminate mankind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.560
it is imperative to eliminate mankind&nbsp;
or release another K-Class Event.”

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:34.400
Oh boy. It seems that the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
of R-42 was not eliminated by SCP-001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:43.120
they eliminated themselves to contain SCP-001. Is&nbsp;
this paradimension faced with this decision now?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.520
The containment procedures of the SCP&nbsp;
file continue on this note. The only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:54.720
way to contain SCP-001 and prevent a ZK-Class&nbsp;
cross-reality failure event is the annihilation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:00.880
of humankind. K Class scenarios are not a&nbsp;
concept used lightly by the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:05.440
We’re familar with the Omega K class&nbsp;
scenario where we are completely rid of death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:11.360
or XK-Class End of the World scenarios, so we&nbsp;
know the danger these anomalies hold to humankind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:17.120
normalcy, and the world. The SCP Foundation&nbsp;
will do anything to prevent these scenarios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:23.600
from occurring, apparently even including the&nbsp;
elimination of all humankind or entire universes.&nbsp;

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:30.800
The description goes more in-depth on the&nbsp;
SCP-001 anomaly. SCP-001 consists of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:37.920
living members of the Homo sapiens species living&nbsp;
within dimension R-42 and the Paradimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:44.080
or PD for short. It seems as though this anomaly&nbsp;
was created out of a mistake from dimension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:49.760
R-42 and PD, as the description states&nbsp;
“The anomaly first came into existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:55.680
and developed in the relict dimension R-42,&nbsp;
and later activated in PD by accident.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.720
How could this have happened? Are these dimensions&nbsp;
linked much more closely than we first thought?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.560
Let’s continue with the description&nbsp;
to find more information. Scarily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.560
this portion of the description contains a&nbsp;
note that states that unchecked growth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:16.240
SCP-001 will cause the annihilation of the entire&nbsp;
multiverse. The SCP Foundations of dimensions R-42&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.520
and PD are not met with this decision,&nbsp;
as now the entire multiverse is at risk.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:26.800
The R-42 SCP Foundation has done immense&nbsp;
research on the topic of the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:32.720
of their universe. After the Big Bang a&nbsp;
finite number of universes were created,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:40.080
only 57 to be exact. However, only one dimension&nbsp;
was able to form humanity, dimension R-42,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.440
and it is unknown why this happened, but all&nbsp;
we know is that with the destruction of R-42&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.600
and the potential annihilation of PD, humanity&nbsp;
will cease to exist in the multiverse.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:57.840
The danger of SCP-001 is that it has the&nbsp;
anomalous capability for wide-scale replication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:04.240
of paradimensions. We are reading this article&nbsp;
from one of these paradimensions, so this SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:10.560
Foundation is technically an anomaly that must&nbsp;
contain itself. A paradimension is defined as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:15.760
parallel reality that has an extremely small&nbsp;
deviation from its parent dimension, in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:22.640
case PD is a paradimension of R-42. It seems that&nbsp;
these paradimensions form as a result of human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:28.320
decision making. So if you’ve ever been between a&nbsp;
type of shirt to buy or were confused on an exam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:34.080
and guessed a question, a paradimension could have&nbsp;
formed from this decision, where the paradimension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:40.640
has you take the other choice. Because of this,&nbsp;
dimensions housing living instances of SCP-001&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:46.640
uncontrollably "grow" a colossal number of&nbsp;
minimally differing paradimensions every second.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:51.200
No sign of paradimensions have been&nbsp;
found in the other 56 parent dimensions.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.600
The picture on this file shows&nbsp;
how PD has branched from R-42,&nbsp;

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:01.360
but at this point, it seems that millions if&nbsp;
not billions or trillions of paradimensions now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:06.800
exist. The real problem of Paradimensions is&nbsp;
that the multiverse has a limit on the number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:12.480
of paradimensions that can exist, and once&nbsp;
this is crossed, the ZK-Class cross-reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:18.640
failure event will begin and the multiverse&nbsp;
will be destroyed. The R-42 dimension’s SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:24.000
Foundation has also discovered that once&nbsp;
humankind emerges in the paradimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:29.120
they can begin to have paradimensions&nbsp;
themselves. The ZK-Class cross-reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:35.840
failure event can be expected to begin between 4&nbsp;
to 2 months from the PD receiving this message.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:42.960
To summarize, SCP-001 is humankind,&nbsp;
specifically its decision-making.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:48.880
When a person makes a decision, a paradimension&nbsp;
may be created. The multiverse has a limit on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:54.240
the number of paradimensions it can have, and&nbsp;
since paradimensions can have paradimensions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.480
they are quickly approaching this&nbsp;
ZK-Class cross-reality failure event.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:04.880
The SCP Foundation of R-42 is approximately&nbsp;
17 years ahead of PD, which allowed them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:10.800
research and develop containment procedures to&nbsp;
contain the anomaly and save the multiverse.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:16.880
R-42’s SCP Foundation discovered SCP-001&nbsp;
five years before writing the file we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:23.200
reading now. And from that, they developed&nbsp;
two Operations: "Castling" and "Minimal Gain"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:28.640
to slow paradimension creation and prevent&nbsp;
the ZK-Class cross-reality failure event.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:33.600
In stage one of Operation Minimal Gain,&nbsp;
the Foundation began with neutralizing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:39.200
decommissioning all of their contained anomalies&nbsp;
under the classification of Euclid or Keter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.920
specifically those that were expensive to&nbsp;
contain or required high levels of personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:48.000
and researchers. Stage Two saw&nbsp;
Operation Castling be commenced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:54.480
the R-42 SCP Foundation launched rockets with&nbsp;
"Variant C-Global" amnestic-dispersing warheads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.040 --> 00:13:00.640
took control of all countries in order to&nbsp;
hold power over all humankind. In Stage 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:04.320
the Foundation began to move their&nbsp;
world to a more natural state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:10.560
destroying all hazardous radioactive, chemical&nbsp;
and bacteriological objects, removing dams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:18.080
and stopping oil extractions. During Stage three,&nbsp;
Stage Four began. The R-42 SCP Foundation began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:24.240
eliminating humanity in third-world countries by&nbsp;
use of viral and biological attacks. Stage Five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:30.000
was a wider spread attack on humanity, where the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation added deactivation-resistant viral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.320
agents to water treatment and collection plants,&nbsp;
food products, medications, and household items&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:42.560
of developed countries. By Stage Six, only 0.1%&nbsp;
of humanity remained and they were targetted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:48.560
drone strikes or put into concentration camps&nbsp;
for elimination. Stage Seven: of the remaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:54.080
survivors the Foundation sampled them to find&nbsp;
the fittest of those left to preserve humankind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.080 --> 00:14:00.240
Stage Eight saw 15,000 of these people put into an&nbsp;
indefinite cryosleep and the remaining survivors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:06.240
were eliminated. Stage Nine saw the destruction&nbsp;
of the remaining SCP Foundation personnel.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:11.040
We move on to a list of proposals that were&nbsp;
made before or during Operations "Castling"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:17.040
and "Minimal Gain". Proposals rejected include,&nbsp;
the use of SCP-objects or other technologies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:21.120
eliminate derivative dimensions, the&nbsp;
development of nanorobots with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:26.080
capability to control human decision-making&nbsp;
capabilities and eliminate variability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:31.600
full replacement of humanity with bionic hybrids&nbsp;
acting explicitly within standard behavioral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:37.360
models, unification of humanity into a neural&nbsp;
network with control given to an AI control unit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:42.880
and the destruction of Earth and/or all of its&nbsp;
inhabitants. While most of these seem like clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:47.840
solutions that would prevent the elimination&nbsp;
of humanity at the SCP Foundation’s hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:54.480
these proposals were all rejected for one reason:&nbsp;
The SCP Foundation did not have enough time.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:15:02.640
One proposal was accepted, however, the use&nbsp;
of SCP-0000. This appears to be the solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:10.640
the R-42 SCP Foundation concocted to fight&nbsp;
SCP-001 and potentially save the multiverse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:18.480
It poses the question, if the R-42 SCP&nbsp;
Foundation used this anomaly to contain SCP-001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:23.040
as proven by the fact they no&nbsp;
longer exist, will PD do the same?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:29.440
The file explains that the R-42 SCP Foundation&nbsp;
opened a dimensional wormhole into PD, as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:34.640
did not know at the time if paradimensions could&nbsp;
cause the creation of more paradimensions. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:41.120
doing this, the SCP Foundation seemingly infected&nbsp;
PD with the ability to create paradimensions. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:47.760
author of this file goes on to explain that&nbsp;
the R-42 SCP Foundation had plans to attack PD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:51.680
and use Operations "Castling" and&nbsp;
"Minimal Gain" in the dimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:56.640
however, they could not access the dimension again&nbsp;
and they believed that the Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:02.800
of PD would have made use of Thaumiel class&nbsp;
anomalies to save themselves and their world.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:09.040
A note from R-42’s Overseer Council is left for&nbsp;
PD. If the Apollyon designation was not enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:13.120
the Overseer council is involved.&nbsp;
The importance of the neutralization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:17.920
of this anomaly can not be forgotten,&nbsp;
so the Overseer Council explain to PD:

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:26.240
“The world has existed before us and must remain&nbsp;
after us. Our multiverse is ill, and the name of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:37.840
the illness is humanity, SCP-001. The only way out&nbsp;
is SCP-0000. We'll cease to become a threat with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:44.640
its help. It is in our power to leave a chance&nbsp;
for other sapient species that, perhaps, will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:51.200
not be afflicted by the same anomaly, or will find&nbsp;
a way to get rid of it before it's too late. We,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:59.360
the O5 Council and other survivors from R-42, have&nbsp;
chosen our fate. We hope you will do the same.”

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:06.960
What is this SCP-0000? How did the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation of R-42 find this solution?

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:17.520
The file for SCP-0000 is placed within this&nbsp;
SCP-001 file. SCP-0000 is a Paradox-Thaumiel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:24.560
class anomaly without any containment&nbsp;
procedures. SCP-0000 is a device that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:28.800
once activated, will destroy the&nbsp;
universe it was activated in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:34.160
It will also destroy all paradimensions&nbsp;
that are not creating other paradimensions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:40.240
As such, PD would not be destroyed, however the&nbsp;
billions or trillions of other paradimensions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:45.840
the R-42 parent dimension created will be&nbsp;
destroyed. PD is left with this harrowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:52.160
decision to continue living, or destroy&nbsp;
itself to save the rest of the multiverse.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:59.840
In the file, a note from R-42’s Joan Simpson is&nbsp;
written for an SCP Foundation Overseer, O5-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:05.760
As part of Operations "Castling" and "Minimal&nbsp;
Gain", the remaining Foundation employees were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:13.360
allowed one family member to uphold morale. Joan&nbsp;
is not writing for R-42’s O5-1, instead, she’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:21.120
writing for PD’s O5-1, this dimension’s version&nbsp;
of her father. She begins with wondering whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:28.000
she can call this version of O5-1 her father, as&nbsp;
her version of her father recently passed away.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:32.720
She remembers the day the Foundation employees&nbsp;
were allowed to choose the one family member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:37.920
they would save for the time being. Her father&nbsp;
was opposed to allowing two family members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:42.240
as he claimed it would cause unnecessary&nbsp;
stress and schisms among the remaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:48.480
few-hundred Foundation staff. O5-1 chose to&nbsp;
have Joan over her mother and she understood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:54.320
everything by the look in his eyes, and grew&nbsp;
angry, but that feeling is long gone now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.920
She began to work with her father and&nbsp;
the remaining Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:03.040
that called themselves hostages behind&nbsp;
the backs of those higher up the ranks.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:09.120
On days she felt sad, Joan and her father would&nbsp;
go up to the surface of the Earth in hazmat suits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:15.200
sitting on the grass and watching over the empty&nbsp;
city at the bottom of the mountain. No humanity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:21.040
remained, with the only life she could see being&nbsp;
birds. Her father promised her that they’d return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:28.000
there and build a giant monument to humanity at&nbsp;
the center of the city. She knew this was a lie.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.360
Joan remembers when someone proposed&nbsp;
that they should open a portal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:37.520
the one that opened to PD. This was their fatal&nbsp;
mistake, as after that the paradimension began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:42.560
replicating paradimensions. The countdown&nbsp;
went down to months again and the promise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:49.200
he made to his daughter became impossible.&nbsp;
O5-1 died and left the position vacant.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:54.960
Joan says to the PD’s O5-1 that she doesn’t&nbsp;
care whether they destroy their world or not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.960 --> 00:20:00.240
or whether the universe will continue to&nbsp;
exist or if there will be new life in it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:02.880
Her world was crushed long ago.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.280
The note also reads the following:

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:10.320
“It's good that this message is encrypted with&nbsp;
your key, that was passed on to me - or these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:16.080
lines would've been deleted. Everyone wants&nbsp;
to save the world. But who needs it like this?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:21.280
Empty and cold. Without those to&nbsp;
appreciate its beauty. Without humanity.”

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.120
“Do whatever you think is right.”

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.880
“I truly feel better now.”

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:28.480
“Love you. Faithfully yours, Joan Simpson.”

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:33.040
We’re not too sure if PD went through with&nbsp;
destroying their universe to save the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:37.840
but it seems that whatever decision was made&nbsp;
would cause the destruction of that universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:44.560
whether that be through the use of SCP-0000&nbsp;
or the ZK-Class cross-reality failure event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:52.080
humanity will cease. But maybe if they make&nbsp;
the decision to use SCP-0000, sapient life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:59.040
can begin to exist again, and hopefully, no&nbsp;
paradimensions will be made from their decisions.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:04.160
Decisions are an extremely innate part of&nbsp;
humanity. You decided to get out of bed this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:10.240
morning. You decided to open up your computer or&nbsp;
phone, and you decided to watch this video. Who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:15.680
knows the amount of paradimensions we may have&nbsp;
created today, but in our world, we’re not at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:23.520
risk, but in the SCP Foundation’s universe,&nbsp;
anything can be anomalous, even humanity.

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:27.760
Now go check out “SCP-507 -&nbsp;
Reluctant Dimension Hopper”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:33.440
and “SCP-2935 - O, Death” for more&nbsp;
Multiverse madness and explanations!

